WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:03.899
Heads up, major Deadpool 2 spoilers ahead.

00:00:03.899 --> 00:00:08.700
The highly-anticipated Deadpool sequel was
chock-full of surprising cameos: Matt Damon

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.889
was tucked in as a redneck with a wealth of
bathroom-related knowledge, Brad Pitt had

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:17.220
a blink-and-you-miss-it appearance as the
invisible hero Vanisher, and even Ryan Reynolds

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.930
took on an additional role, popping up as
the voice of Juggernaut.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:24.800
But by the looks of it, there may have been
was another character cameo hidden in the

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.990
sequel, none other than the Joker himself.

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:29.530
"You sure you're not from the DC universe?"

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:33.530
When Deadpool and Russell are shipped off
to the criminal-packed prison called the Icebox,

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:37.250
the pair meet a hodgepodge of dangerous bad
guys and random freaks.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:41.590
But if fans look closely in the crowd, they'll
spot a man who looks uncannily like Jared

00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:42.700
Leto's Joker.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.180
He's got the white skin and bright green hair,
and no close Marvel character comparisons.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.570
It's hard to argue that he isn't DC's Clown
Prince of Crime.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:54.420
There are two extra bits of evidence throughout
the film that bolster the argument that Joker

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.610
made an appearance.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:59.460
The first is a gun that's shown with a "bang!"
flag popping out of its barrel, which looks

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:04.299
kinda similar to the flag that's flung out
of the Joker's gun in Tim Burton's 1989 Batman

00:01:04.299 --> 00:01:05.299
movie.

00:01:05.299 --> 00:01:09.750
The second comes during the sequence in which
Cable asks Deadpool to identify himself, Deadpool

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:14.580
cheekily responds, "I'm Batman," using a voice
that sounds like former Batman actor Michael

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.580
Keaton's.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.540
At the end of the day, either the team behind
the Deadpool sequel included the iconic villain

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:23.200
but won't admit to it because Warner Brothers
holds the rights to the character, or this

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.530
is all just one big coincidence.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:29.380
Fans can decide for themselves when they catch
Deadpool 2 in a repeat viewing.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:30.380
Thanks for watching!

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.560
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.420
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

